  "purpose": {
    "classification": "DECLARED",
    "text": "Desktop capture contracts and bounded callback delivery.  Platform code owns OS integration, `frame_stream` owns the bounded SPSC crossing, and `capture_owner` owns non-realtime lifecycle. Public capture declarations are data contracts only.  Every native callback follows the same permanent contract: acquire from a fixed-capacity pool, write through non-panicking fixed-slot APIs, publish with a nonblocking bounded send, and account for rejection. Callback code must not allocate, lock, block, await, log, or unwind."
  },
